\p{Some more theory on modalities. In particular of orthogonal maps:}


\ul{
  \li{Defines orthogonal maps and generally more theory about arrows \ref{Core.Orthogonal}, \ref{Core.Arrows}, \ref{Core.ArrowEquiv}}
  \li{Characterises a number of equivalent conditions for orthogonality
       \ref{stt-004A}}
  \li{Defines factorisations: \ref{Modalities.Factorisations}}
  \li{Defines orthogonal factorisation systems: \ref{Modalities.OrthogonalFactorisationSystems}}
  \li{Gives first example of a modality \ref{Modalities.Instances.Open}}
}
